One of the key strengths of BiTCN lies in its ability to capture long-range dependencies through the use of dilated convolutions. This allows the model to access a broader temporal context without increasing computational complexity. Additionally, BiTCN preserves the temporal order of sequence data, which is critical in biological sequences where the arrangement of amino acids determines functional and structural properties. Importantly, BiTCN processes input in both forward and backward directions, enabling the model to extract contextual information from both preceding and succeeding residues. The output of each BiTCN is computed by combining the results of forward and backward TCN passes, typically as follows:23\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
